course: dictionary
lesson: 8331
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The word roller is one of them. A roller is a tube or cylinder that turns. To find out which meaning fits, look at the words around it. «A conveyor belt is a long loop of rubber or metal pulled round by motors and rollers» tells you the rollers are turning parts that carry the belt.
explain: The clues can also point to a ride. «A roller coaster car stays on the track upside down in a loop because it is going fast enough» is about a fast ride, not a tube. The same word can mean something different in each sentence, so always read the whole sentence first.
explain: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. Try «A tube that turns» in «Printed pictures are printed by fast rollers.» It fits, because fast rollers turn and press ink onto paper. When it does not fit, try another meaning.
fact: A roller is a tube or cylinder that turns.
fact: A paint roller is a tool for painting walls.
fact: A hair roller, also called a curler, is a small tube that curls hair.
fact: A roller can also be a big wave rolling in from the sea, or a heavy machine that flattens roads or ground.
fact: Rollers help heavy things move more easily, because they turn instead of rubbing.
exercise: «A conveyor belt is a long loop of rubber or metal pulled round by motors and rollers.» In this sentence, what is a roller? | A big wave from the sea | A pen for animals | A type of sock | *A tube or cylinder that turns
exercise: «Printed pictures in books and magazines are printed one after another by fast rollers.» What do the rollers do? | *They turn and press ink onto paper | They hold the pages still | They sing while the book is read | They warm the room
exercise: «A roller coaster car stays on the track upside down in a loop because it is going fast enough.» What is a roller coaster? | A heavy machine for flattening roads | A slow boat for canals | A tube for curling hair | *A fast ride with a track that loops
test: Which tool is used to paint the walls of a room? | *A paint roller | A roller blind | A hair roller | A roller coaster
test: What does a heavy roller do on a road? | Lights it up | *Flattens the road or ground | Waters the plants | Paints lines on it
exam: Which meaning of roller fits «The hair roller kept her curls in all night»? | A heavy machine for flattening roads | *A small tube that curls hair | A tool for painting walls | A big wave rolling in from the sea
